-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 7, §7.3 סגן מנהל
-- The deputy principal: the work unit and its teaching and management
-- hours, the reform's protection of management hours, how many deputies a
-- school's classes justify, the threshold qualifications, the selection
-- procedures, further roles, the trial period and removal, the rewards
-- (management, telephone, travel) and management seniority.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions

§ `7.3 סגן מנהל`

@desc The kinds of institution section 7.3 distinguishes.
DECLARE `kind of institution` IS ONE OF
    `primary school`
    `post-primary school including a middle school`
    `independent middle school`
    `special education school`
    `teacher training institution`

@desc A deputy principal's post, as far as section 7.3.1 asks.
DECLARE `deputy post` HAS
    `institution`                       IS A `kind of institution`
    `teacher's work unit in the institution` IS A NUMBER @desc the weekly hours of a teacher's work unit in that kind of institution, set elsewhere in the takanon
    `teaching hours`                    IS A NUMBER
    `management hours`                  IS A NUMBER

@desc A principal or deputy of a primary school whose grades 7–8 moved to a middle school in the reform.
DECLARE `reform-affected manager` HAS
    `classes lost to the middle school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the school's classes were reduced by moving grades 7–8 to the middle school in the reform
    `day of the reform`                 IS A DATE @desc the day the reform was carried out at the school
    `age on the day of the reform`      IS A NUMBER
    `management hours before`           IS A NUMBER
    `teaching hours before`             IS A NUMBER
    `management hours the reduced school gives` IS A NUMBER @desc the management hours the school's reduced number of classes would give

@desc Who acts in section 7.3.
DECLARE `7.3 party` IS ONE OF
    `the selection committee` @desc the internal selection committee of (3) 2.2.1
    `the district manager`
    `a candidate`
    `the appointing body` @desc whoever gives the notice of section 3.5; the text names no one (F-7.3-b)
    `the principal`
    `the school supervisor`
    `the district supervisor`
    `the head of state-religious education or his representative`
    `the representative organisation's representative`
    `a headquarters representative`
    `the external selection committee` @desc the committee of (3) 2.3.2
    `the Pais selection committee` @desc the committee of (5) 3.4
    `the advisers' committee` @desc named in (2)א only (F-7.3-h)
    `the district`
    `the local authority's representative`
    `the district science and technology supervisor`
    `a science and technology administration representative`
    `the Ministry's district office`
    `the school's owner`

DECLARE `7.3 action` IS ONE OF
    `submit recommendations to the district manager`
    `appoint a selection committee`
    `apply for the post` HAS `meets the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `give a reasoned written notice of not being invited to interview`
    `ask the supervisor to approve an internal selection procedure`
    `answer the request to approve an internal selection procedure`
    `post a notice of the vacancy on the school's notice board`
    `approve or reject the recommendations and notify the candidates, with copies`
    `publish a notice of the vacancy in the press`
    `complete the external selection`
    `post a notice of the vacancy on the cluster's schools' notice boards`
    `report on the deputy's work to the general supervisor, with a recommendation`
    `send notice of ending the deputy's work`

§§ `7.3.1 יחידת עבודה`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p2 The heading of §7.3.1 (work unit).
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p3 An amendment note: the section was updated on 30.1.03.

-- §7.3.1(1): a deputy teaches at least 12 hours in grades 1–14, or 10 in an
-- independent middle school, or 4 in a teacher training institution. An
-- independent middle school's grades are within 1–14; its own figure (10)
-- is read as the rule for it (F-7.3-c).
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p4
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minimum teaching hours of a deputy` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `independent middle school`    THEN 10
    WHEN `teacher training institution` THEN 4
    OTHERWISE 12

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p4
GIVEN d IS A `deputy post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deputy's work unit is made up as required` d IF
        d's `teaching hours` PLUS d's `management hours` EQUALS d's `teacher's work unit in the institution`
    AND d's `teaching hours` AT LEAST `minimum teaching hours of a deputy` (d's `institution`)

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p5
GIVEN d IS A `deputy post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `maximum management hours` d IS
    d's `teacher's work unit in the institution` MINUS `minimum teaching hours of a deputy` (d's `institution`)

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p6 The heading of §7.3.1(2) (management hours); its paragraphs are encoded below.

-- (2)א: management hours lost with the classes become teaching hours, hour
-- for hour, "notwithstanding" which (2)ב protects one aged 50 or more.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p8
GIVEN m IS A `reform-affected manager`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `management hours after the reform` m IS
    IF m's `classes lost to the middle school` AND NOT `(2)ב protects his management and teaching hours` m
    THEN min (m's `management hours before`) (m's `management hours the reduced school gives`)
    ELSE m's `management hours before`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p8
GIVEN m IS A `reform-affected manager`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `teaching hours after the reform` m IS
    m's `teaching hours before` PLUS (m's `management hours before` MINUS `management hours after the reform` m)

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p8
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `turning management hours into teaching hours is a worsening of conditions` IF FALSE

-- (2)ב, in force from 1.9.69: a principal or deputy of a primary school aged
-- 50 or more on the day of the reform keeps his management hours and his
-- teaching hours. "תחולה 1.9.69" is read as the day of the reform: a
-- reform carried out before it is not protected (F-7.3-e).
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p9
GIVEN m IS A `reform-affected manager`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `(2)ב protects his management and teaching hours` m IF
        m's `classes lost to the middle school`
    AND m's `age on the day of the reform` AT LEAST 50
    AND (m's `day of the reform` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969))

-- (2)ג, in force from 1.9.92: a principal or deputy aged 50 or more on the
-- day of the reform whose grades 7–8 moved to the middle school keeps his
-- position base, 24, in teaching and in management hours, as it was before
-- the move.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p10 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p11
`the position base (2)ג keeps` MEANS 24

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p10 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p11
GIVEN m IS A `reform-affected manager`, `the month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeps his position base in teaching and management hours as before the move` m `the month` IF
        m's `classes lost to the middle school`
    AND m's `age on the day of the reform` AT LEAST 50
    AND (`the month` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1992))

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p12 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p13 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p14 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 7.3.1.

§§ `7.3.2 מינוי`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p15 The heading of §7.3.2 (appointment).
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p16 The heading of §7.3.2(1) (the number of classes that justifies a deputy); its table is encoded below.

-- §7.3.2(1)'s table as printed: the classes at which a first, second and
-- third deputy may be appointed, "and so on" (וכן הלאה) beyond the third.
-- A special education school is under (ג) whatever its level.
@desc One row of section 7.3.2(1): the numbers of classes from which a first, second and third deputy may be appointed.
DECLARE `deputy thresholds` HAS
    `classes for a first deputy`  IS A NUMBER
    `classes for a second deputy` IS A NUMBER
    `classes for a third deputy`  IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p17 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p18 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p19 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p20 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p22 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p23 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p24 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p25 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p26 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p27 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p28 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p29 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p30 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p31 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p32 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p33
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A `deputy thresholds`
DECIDE `thresholds for` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `primary school`               THEN `deputy thresholds` 12 21 30
    WHEN `teacher training institution` THEN `deputy thresholds` 7 14 21
    OTHERWISE                                `deputy thresholds` 10 19 28

-- The deputies the printed rows give: none, first, second or third.
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, `classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deputies the printed rows allow` k `classes` IS
    BRANCH IF `classes` AT LEAST (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a third deputy`  THEN 3
           IF `classes` AT LEAST (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a second deputy` THEN 2
           IF `classes` AT LEAST (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a first deputy`  THEN 1
           OTHERWISE 0

-- F-7.3-a: beyond the third deputy the table says only "וכן הלאה". The
-- printed rows give no number of classes for a fourth deputy: a primary
-- school of 39 or of 60 classes is given the same three.
`the table gives no fourth deputy's threshold` MEANS
        `deputies the printed rows allow` `primary school` 39 EQUALS 3
    AND `deputies the printed rows allow` `primary school` 60 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the table gives no fourth deputy's threshold`

-- The reading adopted (F-7.3-a): "and so on" continues each row's own step
-- (9 classes for primary, post-primary and special education schools; 7 for
-- teacher training), so each further step justifies one more deputy.
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, `classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deputies the institution may have` k `classes` IS
    IF `classes` LESS THAN (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a first deputy`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 1 PLUS TRUNC ((`classes` MINUS (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a first deputy`)
                       DIVIDED BY ((`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a second deputy` MINUS (`thresholds for` k)'s `classes for a first deputy`)) 0

-- The note to (1)א: a primary school's young-division classes are taken
-- off its classes for appointing deputies and for their reward.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p21
GIVEN `all classes` IS A NUMBER, `young division classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `classes counted for deputies` `all classes` `young division classes` IS
    `all classes` MINUS `young division classes`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p34 The heading of §7.3.2(2) (threshold qualifications for a deputy and for a Pais cluster manager); the qualifications are encoded below.
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p35 The label "נספח 6" over the qualifications, the circular annex they come from.

@desc A candidate's pedagogical qualification, as the alternatives of §7.3.2(2)א(1) and ב(1) name them.
DECLARE `pedagogical qualification` IS ONE OF
    `a certified or senior certified teacher's certificate from a recognised Israeli institution`
    `certification by supplementary examinations`
    `a permanent teaching licence for post-primary education`
    `a licence to practise teaching`
    `an Israeli university teaching certificate`
    `an educational leadership school graduate's certificate`
    `a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary track`
    `a licence in educational counselling`
    `no pedagogical qualification`

@desc A candidate for a deputy's post, as far as the threshold qualifications ask.
DECLARE `deputy candidate` HAS
    `qualification`                       IS A `pedagogical qualification`
    `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the licensing process was completed, or eligibility for the licence confirmed, by the last day for submitting the candidacy form
    `holds a recognised academic degree`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc from a recognised Israeli institution, or a foreign one with an equivalence approval
    `holds at least a first degree`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds at least an M.A.`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `years teaching in primary or post-primary grades 7-12` IS A NUMBER @desc years of actual teaching in Israel, at a scope that earns seniority, in which the candidate succeeded; not lecturing or tutoring at a university or college, not coordinating Perach
    `years teaching in post-primary grades 7-12 or grades 7-8 of a primary school` IS A NUMBER @desc same measure, in these grades only
    `years teaching in teacher training institutions` IS A NUMBER @desc years of teaching in teacher training institutions, having filled successfully the roles the head of the institution gave
    `certified for special education`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc the certification of chapter 4 (4.2), "teaching employees in special education"

-- (2)א(1): one of the listed qualifications; a leadership-school
-- certificate counts as a teaching certificate. In the licence alternative
-- the licence must be in hand (or its eligibility confirmed) by the
-- candidacy deadline, and a counselling licence is not a teaching licence.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p36 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p37 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p38
GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the primary school's pedagogical requirement` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `qualification`
    WHEN `a certified or senior certified teacher's certificate from a recognised Israeli institution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `certification by supplementary examinations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Israeli university teaching certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an educational leadership school graduate's certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a permanent teaching licence for post-primary education` THEN c's `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline`
    WHEN `a licence to practise teaching` THEN c's `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline`
    WHEN `a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary track` THEN c's `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline`
    WHEN `a licence in educational counselling` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no pedagogical qualification` THEN FALSE

-- (2)א(2)-(3): a recognised academic degree (Torah learning is desirable
-- in a religious school, and decides nothing), and at least 5 years of
-- actual, successful teaching in primary or post-primary grades 7-12 in
-- Israel. (2)א(4): in a special education school, special education
-- certification as well.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p36 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p39 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p40
GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c IF
        `meets the primary school's pedagogical requirement` c
    AND c's `holds a recognised academic degree`
    AND c's `years teaching in primary or post-primary grades 7-12` AT LEAST 5

-- (2)ב: a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary
-- track, in hand by the deadline (a counselling licence does not count); at
-- least a first degree; at least 5 years of actual, successful teaching in
-- post-primary grades 7-12 or grades 7-8 of a primary school.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p50 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p51 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p52 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p53 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p54
GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold for a middle or post-primary school deputy` c IF
        c's `qualification` EQUALS `a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary track`
    AND c's `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline`
    AND c's `holds at least a first degree`
    AND c's `years teaching in post-primary grades 7-12 or grades 7-8 of a primary school` AT LEAST 5

-- (2)א(4) and (2)ג say the same: a special education school's deputy meets
-- the primary school's threshold and is certified for special education.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p41 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p55 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p56
GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold for a special education school deputy` c IF
        `meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c
    AND c's `certified for special education`

-- (2)ד: in a seminary for women teachers and kindergarten teachers, a
-- teaching employee with at least an M.A. and 5 years of teaching in
-- teacher training institutions; the colleges are not bound to appoint a
-- deputy at all.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p57 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p58
GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold for a teacher training institution deputy` c IF
        c's `holds at least an M.A.`
    AND c's `years teaching in teacher training institutions` AT LEAST 5

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p58
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a college must appoint a deputy` IF FALSE

-- The threshold that applies by kind of institution. An independent middle
-- school and a post-primary school are (2)ב's. F-7.3-i: the heading of (2)
-- promises thresholds for a Pais cluster manager too, and none is given;
-- the cluster is attached to a six-year school or an independent middle
-- school (§3.4), and the reading adopted is (2)ב's.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p36 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p50 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p55 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p57
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold qualifications` k c IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `primary school` THEN `meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c
    WHEN `post-primary school including a middle school` THEN `meets the threshold for a middle or post-primary school deputy` c
    WHEN `independent middle school` THEN `meets the threshold for a middle or post-primary school deputy` c
    WHEN `special education school` THEN `meets the threshold for a special education school deputy` c
    WHEN `teacher training institution` THEN `meets the threshold for a teacher training institution deputy` c

GIVETH A LIST OF `pedagogical qualification`
DECIDE `the threshold qualifications (2) gives for a Pais cluster manager` IS EMPTY

`(2) gives a Pais cluster manager no qualifications of his own` MEANS
    `the threshold qualifications (2) gives for a Pais cluster manager` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `(2) gives a Pais cluster manager no qualifications of his own`

GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold for a Pais cluster manager` c IF
    `meets the threshold for a middle or post-primary school deputy` c

-- The desirable qualifications, (2)א and ד: weighed by the committee in
-- forming its recommendation, and required of no one. F-7.3-h: "ועדת
-- היועצים" (the advisers' committee) is defined nowhere in the section;
-- read as the selection committee of (3).
@desc The desirable qualifications (2)א and ד list.
DECLARE `desirable qualification` IS ONE OF
    `ability to guide pedagogical work and activity outside the curriculum`
    `knowledge of the Ministry's instructions in a deputy's fields`
    `ability to express oneself in Hebrew, and in the school's language of instruction`
    `ability to negotiate with parents and pupils`
    `ability to keep proper working relations`
    `a certificate from a school-management training programme`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p42 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p43 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p44 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p45 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p46 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p47 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p48 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p49 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p59 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p60 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p61 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p62 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p63 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p64 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p65 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p66
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, c IS A `deputy candidate`, d IS A LIST OF `desirable qualification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible, whatever desirable qualifications are held` k c d IF
    `meets the threshold qualifications` k c

`the committees section 7.3 constitutes` MEANS LIST `the selection committee`, `the external selection committee`, `the Pais selection committee`
`the advisers' committee is one of them` MEANS elem `the advisers' committee` `the committees section 7.3 constitutes`
`the advisers' committee is constituted nowhere` MEANS NOT `the advisers' committee is one of them`
#ASSERT `the advisers' committee is constituted nowhere`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p67 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p68 (2)ה, a school for practical engineers and technicians: a pointer to §9.11, encoded there.
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3/p69 The heading of (3), appointing deputies in official schools.
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3 The headings of 2.1 (general), 2.2 (internal selection) and 2.3 (external selection).

-- 2.1: when the classes reach the number that justifies a deputy, the
-- principal asks the supervisor to approve an internal selection; the
-- answer is given "עד חודש פברואר" of that year, for a deputy of the next
-- school year. F-7.3-f: "(ראה נספח7)" points to an annex the section does
-- not hold; read as §7.3.2(1)'s table, which gives that number.
-- F-7.3-m: "עד חודש פברואר" is read as by the end of February.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_1/p1
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, `classes` IS A NUMBER, `deputies in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `asking for an internal selection` k `classes` `deputies in office` IS
    IF `deputies the institution may have` k `classes` GREATER THAN `deputies in office`
    THEN PARTY `the principal`
         MAY   `ask the supervisor to approve an internal selection procedure`
    ELSE FULFILLED

`the annexes section 7.3 holds` MEANS LIST 6
`(3) 2.1 points to an annex 7 the section does not hold` MEANS NOT (elem 7 `the annexes section 7.3 holds`)
#ASSERT `(3) 2.1 points to an annex 7 the section does not hold`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_1/p1
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last day for the supervisor's answer` y IS
    DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 y) MINUS 1

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_1/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `answering the request` IS
    PARTY `the school supervisor`
    MUST  `answer the request to approve an internal selection procedure`

`February's two readings differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the last day for the supervisor's answer` 2026 EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026))
#ASSERT `February's two readings differ`

-- 2.2.1: the vacancy is posted on the school's notice board no later than
-- the last week of February, with the qualifications, the dates and the
-- procedures; any teacher of the school who meets the requirements may
-- apply; the committee has two members, the principal and the school's
-- supervisor. F-7.3-g: two members, and no rule for when they disagree
-- (3.4 gives its own committee a casting vote); read as no recommendation.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `posting the internal vacancy` IS
    PARTY `the principal`
    MUST  `post a notice of the vacancy on the school's notice board`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_1
GIVEN `a teacher of the school` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply in the internal selection` `a teacher of the school` `meets the requirements` IF
    `a teacher of the school` AND `meets the requirements`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_1
`the internal committee's members` MEANS LIST `the principal`, `the school supervisor`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_1
GIVEN `principal recommends` IS A BOOLEAN, `supervisor recommends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internal committee recommends` `principal recommends` `supervisor recommends` IF
    `principal recommends` AND `supervisor recommends`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internal committee has a casting vote` IF FALSE
`a two-member committee may split with no rule to decide` MEANS
    count `the internal committee's members` EQUALS 2 AND NOT `the internal committee has a casting vote`
#ASSERT `a two-member committee may split with no rule to decide`

-- 2.2.2: the committee's recommendations reach the district manager no
-- later than the third week of March. Time in days from 1 March (day 0).
-- "The third week of March" is read as 15–21 March, the third seven days
-- counted from the 1st, so the recommendations are due by 21 March, day
-- 20, in every year (F-7.3-d).
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_2
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of March's third week` y IS
    DATE_FROM_DMY 21 3 y

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_2
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days from 1 March to the end of its third week` IS
    DATE_SERIAL (`the last day of March's third week` 2026) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026)

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `the internal committee's recommendations` IS
    PARTY `the selection committee`
    MUST  `submit recommendations to the district manager`
    WITHIN `days from 1 March to the end of its third week`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the selection committee` BECAUSE "section 7.3.2, 2.2.2: recommendations by the third week of March"

-- 2.2.3: the district manager approves or rejects; the decision is sent to
-- the candidates, with copies to the senior division for teaching staff and
-- the principal; the procedure ends by the first week of April. Time in
-- days from 1 April (day 0): the first seven days end on day 6.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_3
GIVEN `the district manager approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internal selection appoints` `the district manager approves` IF
    `the district manager approves`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_2_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `deciding on the recommendations` IS
    PARTY `the district manager`
    MUST  `approve or reject the recommendations and notify the candidates, with copies`
    WITHIN 6
    LEST  BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 7.3.2, 2.2.3: the procedure ends by the first week of April"

-- 2.3.1: an external vacancy is published in the press when no teacher of
-- the school is a candidate, or the internal committee recommends no one,
-- or the district manager does not approve; everything below is done by
-- the end of May of that year.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_1
GIVEN `a candidate from the school` IS A BOOLEAN, `the internal committee recommends` IS A BOOLEAN, `the district manager approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an external selection is held` `a candidate from the school` `the internal committee recommends` `the district manager approves` IF
        (NOT `a candidate from the school`)
    OR  (NOT `the internal committee recommends`)
    OR  (NOT `the district manager approves`)

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_1
GIVEN `held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `the external selection` `held` IS
    IF `held`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `publish a notice of the vacancy in the press`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Time in days from 1 March (day 0): the end of May is day 91.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_1
`days from 1 March to the end of May` MEANS 91

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_1
GIVEN `held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `completing the external selection` `held` IS
    IF `held`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `complete the external selection`
         WITHIN `days from 1 March to the end of May`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 7.3.2, 2.3.1: every step is done by the end of May"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 2.3.2: the district manager appoints an external committee: the district
-- supervisor in the chair (in state-religious institutions the head of
-- state-religious education or his representative), the representative
-- organisation's representative, the principal, the school's supervisor
-- and a representative of headquarters.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `the external selection committee` IS
    PARTY `the district manager`
    MUST  `appoint a selection committee`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p1
GIVEN `state-religious institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `7.3 party`
DECIDE `the external committee's chair` `state-religious institution` IS
    IF `state-religious institution`
    THEN `the head of state-religious education or his representative`
    ELSE `the district supervisor`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p5
GIVEN `state-religious institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `7.3 party`
DECIDE `the external committee's members` `state-religious institution` IS
    LIST `the external committee's chair` `state-religious institution`,
         `the representative organisation's representative`,
         `the principal`,
         `the school supervisor`,
         `a headquarters representative`

-- (4), a deputy in office on the day this arrangement was published: one
-- who served 3 full years is permanent in the post; one who served less and
-- meets the qualifications is as if he won the tender; one who served less
-- and does not stops at the end of תשמ"ג; from תשמ"ד the tender rules
-- apply. The day of publication is not stated, and (ג)–(ד) place it in
-- תשמ"ג; years of service are an input.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p6 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p8 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p9 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p10 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p11
DECLARE `veteran deputy's standing` IS ONE OF
    `permanent in the post`
    `as if he won the tender`
    `his work stops at the end of תשמ"ג`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p8 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p9 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p10
GIVEN `years served on the day of publication` IS A NUMBER, `meets the qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `veteran deputy's standing`
DECIDE `a veteran deputy's standing` `years served on the day of publication` `meets the qualifications` IS
    IF `years served on the day of publication` AT LEAST 3
    THEN `permanent in the post`
    ELSE IF `meets the qualifications`
         THEN `as if he won the tender`
         ELSE `his work stops at the end of תשמ"ג`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p11
`the first school year the tender rules govern` MEANS "תשמ\"ד"

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_2_3_2/p12 The heading of (5), selecting Pais cluster managers.

-- (5) 3.1-3.3: the selection and appointment are as for deputies in
-- official schools; the district posts the vacancy, with the
-- qualifications, dates and procedures, on the notice boards of the schools
-- the cluster belongs to; anyone who meets the requirements may apply.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_1
GIVEN `selected and appointed as for deputies in official schools` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the selection followed the procedure` `selected and appointed as for deputies in official schools` IF
    `selected and appointed as for deputies in official schools`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `posting the cluster vacancy` IS
    PARTY `the district`
    MUST  `post a notice of the vacancy on the cluster's schools' notice boards`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `applying for the post` IS
    PARTY `a candidate`
    MAY   `apply for the post` meets PROVIDED meets

-- 3.4: a committee the district manager appoints and chairs (or his
-- representative): the local authority's representative, the principal of
-- the six-year school or independent middle school the cluster is attached
-- to, the representative organisation's representative, the school's
-- supervisor, the district science and technology supervisor, and an
-- observer from the science and technology administration, who does not
-- vote. Without a clear decision the chair's vote decides.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p5 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p6 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p8
`the Pais committee's voting members` MEANS
    LIST `the district manager`,
         `the local authority's representative`,
         `the principal`,
         `the representative organisation's representative`,
         `the school supervisor`,
         `the district science and technology supervisor`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p8
`the Pais committee's observer` MEANS `a science and technology administration representative`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_4/p2
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the chair votes for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Pais committee selects` `votes for` `votes against` `the chair votes for` IF
    IF `votes for` EQUALS `votes against`
    THEN `the chair votes for`
    ELSE `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`

-- 3.5: a candidate not invited to the interview receives a reasoned
-- written notice.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5
GIVEN `invited to interview` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `notice to a candidate not interviewed` `invited to interview` IS
    IF `invited to interview`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the appointing body`
         MUST  `give a reasoned written notice of not being invited to interview`

-- F-7.3-b: the candidate "shall receive" the notice; the text does not say
-- from whom. Read as the body that runs the selection (`the appointing body`).
GIVETH A LIST OF `7.3 party`
DECIDE `the parties section 3.5 names as giving the notice` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3.5 names no one to give the notice` IF
    `the parties section 3.5 names as giving the notice` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 3.5 names no one to give the notice`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p5 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p6 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.2.
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p8 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p9 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p10 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_3_5/p11 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.2, continued.

§§ `7.3.3 תפקידים נוספים`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3/p1 The heading of §7.3.3 and its amendment note (updated 5.2.03).

@desc A further role a deputy may be appointed to, as §7.3.3 names them.
DECLARE `further role` IS ONE OF
    `class educator`
    `security officer`
    `teacher-counsellor`
    `a sixth of a position in guidance`

-- (1) a deputy may also be a class educator or the security officer; (3)
-- never a teacher-counsellor (§3.12.7(8), encoded there); (4) a sixth of a
-- position in guidance is allowed. (2) was cancelled from 1.9.94.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3__para_1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3__para_3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3__para_4
GIVEN r IS A `further role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a deputy may also hold` r IF
    NOT (r EQUALS `teacher-counsellor`)

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3__para_2 (2) is cancelled (from 1.9.94) and carries no rule.

-- (4): with a sixth of a position in guidance the deputy receives, besides
-- the management reward, a sixth of a guiding teacher's reward (an input).
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3__para_4
GIVEN `management reward` IS A NUMBER, `a guiding teacher's reward` IS A NUMBER, `guides a sixth of a position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a deputy's rewards with guidance` `management reward` `a guiding teacher's reward` `guides a sixth of a position` IS
    IF `guides a sixth of a position`
    THEN `management reward` PLUS `a guiding teacher's reward` DIVIDED BY 6
    ELSE `management reward`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_3/p5 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.3.

§§ `7.3.4 תקופת ניסיון, קביעות והפסקת עבודה`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4 The heading of §7.3.4.

-- (6): these provisions apply to primary schools and independent middle
-- schools.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_6
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7.3.4 applies` k IF
    k EQUALS `primary school` OR k EQUALS `independent middle school`

-- (1): the trial period is 3 years; a deputy who completes it receives the
-- district's confirmation that he is permanent in the post.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_1
`the deputy's trial period in years` MEANS 3

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_1
GIVEN `trial years completed` IS A NUMBER, `removed during the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in the post` `trial years completed` `removed during the trial` IF
    `trial years completed` AT LEAST `the deputy's trial period in years` AND NOT `removed during the trial`

-- (2): by 1 April of each trial year the principal reports on the deputy's
-- work to the general supervisor and recommends continuing or ending it
-- (in the third year, permanence or ending); the district manager acts on
-- the recommendation; a notice of ending is sent by 30 May. Time in days
-- from 1 September of the trial year (day 0): 1 April is day 212 in a
-- year whose February has 28 days, 30 May day 271.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `the principal's yearly report` IS
    PARTY `the principal`
    MUST  `report on the deputy's work to the general supervisor, with a recommendation`
    WITHIN 212
    LEST  BREACH BY `the principal` BECAUSE "section 7.3.4(2): the report is due by 1 April of each trial year"

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_2
GIVEN `the principal recommends ending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `7.3 party` `7.3 action`
DECIDE `acting on the recommendation` `the principal recommends ending` IS
    IF `the principal recommends ending`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `send notice of ending the deputy's work`
         WITHIN 271
         LEST  BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 7.3.4(2): the notice of ending is sent by 30 May"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (3)-(5): who may remove a deputy. F-7.3-j: (3) gives the district
-- manager (in state-religious education with its district head's consent)
-- the removal "during the trial period, until the end of the third school
-- year", and (4) gives a parity committee the removal "during the trial
-- period, within the school year"; a removal in the middle of a trial year
-- falls under both. Read as (4) for a removal within a school year and (3)
-- for a removal at a year's end. (5): a permanent deputy is removed by a
-- parity committee, as for permanent teaching employees.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_5
DECLARE `removal authority` IS ONE OF
    `the district manager, after written reports from the principal and the supervisor`
    `a parity committee of the district supervisor and the representative organisation`
    `a parity committee, as for permanent teaching employees`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_4
GIVEN `in the trial period` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the school year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `removal authority`
DECIDE `the authorities the text gives` `in the trial period` `within the school year` IS
    IF `in the trial period`
    THEN IF `within the school year`
         THEN LIST `the district manager, after written reports from the principal and the supervisor`, `a parity committee of the district supervisor and the representative organisation`
         ELSE LIST `the district manager, after written reports from the principal and the supervisor`
    ELSE LIST `a parity committee, as for permanent teaching employees`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4__para_5
GIVEN `in the trial period` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the school year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `removal authority`
DECIDE `who may remove the deputy` `in the trial period` `within the school year` IS
    IF `in the trial period`
    THEN IF `within the school year`
         THEN `a parity committee of the district supervisor and the representative organisation`
         ELSE `the district manager, after written reports from the principal and the supervisor`
    ELSE `a parity committee, as for permanent teaching employees`

`a removal within a trial year has two authorities` MEANS
    count (`the authorities the text gives` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `a removal within a trial year has two authorities`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_4/p2 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.4.

§§ `7.3.5 מילוי מקום`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_5 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_5/p1 §7.3.5 (substitution) points to §1.30, encoded there.

§§ `7.3.6 גמולים`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1 The headings of §7.3.6 (rewards) and §7.3.6.1 (management reward).

-- 7.3.6.1(1): the management reward is a percentage of the deputy's
-- personal combined salary, by "the table below" (from 1.1.98); the table
-- is not in the corpus text, so the percentage is an input. Seniority in
-- management is added (§7.6.10 and §7.3.10). (2): the percentage follows
-- the institution's level and classes, not the position fraction; more
-- than one full position adds nothing. (3): a second and third deputy get
-- the first deputy's reward. (4): an uncertified teacher serving as deputy
-- gets half.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p11 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p13 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p14
GIVEN `personal combined salary` IS A NUMBER
      `the table's percentage for the institution's level and classes` IS A NUMBER @desc from the table §7.3.6.1(1) names, which the corpus text does not carry
      `certified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `position fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc it does not enter: (2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a deputy's management reward` `personal combined salary` `the table's percentage for the institution's level and classes` `certified` `position fraction` IS
    LET full MEANS `personal combined salary` TIMES `the table's percentage for the institution's level and classes`
    IN  IF `certified` THEN full ELSE full DIVIDED BY 2

-- (2)'s clarification: a deputy or principal who receives the management
-- reward as part of his pay in any form (a study year's pay, a pension and
-- the like) and lawfully works a part-time position in teaching or
-- management gets no reward for that part-time work.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p12
GIVEN `receives the management reward in his pay in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reward is paid for a part-time teaching or management position` `receives the management reward in his pay in any form` IF
    NOT `receives the management reward in his pay in any form`

-- (1א): the number of classes of a maritime or agricultural school, for
-- the reward: (standard hours + visiting classes) / 24 or 30, at 2 weekly
-- hours a class; with visiting classes × 1.5 at 3 hours; rounded up; 24 for
-- grades 1-6, 30 for 7 and up; from 1.9.87. F-7.3-l: where 2 and 3 hours
-- are taught together the formula is "calculated accordingly" and not
-- given; read as each visiting class weighted by its own hours, a half per
-- weekly hour.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p3 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p4 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p5 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p6 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p7 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p8 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p9 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p10
GIVEN `standard hours` IS A NUMBER
      `visiting classes at 2 hours` IS A NUMBER
      `visiting classes at 3 hours` IS A NUMBER
      `grades 7 and up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `classes of a maritime or agricultural school` `standard hours` `visiting classes at 2 hours` `visiting classes at 3 hours` `grades 7 and up` IS
    CEILING ((`standard hours` PLUS `visiting classes at 2 hours` PLUS `visiting classes at 3 hours` TIMES 1.5)
             DIVIDED BY (IF `grades 7 and up` THEN 30 ELSE 24))

GIVEN `visiting classes at 2 hours` IS A NUMBER, `visiting classes at 3 hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the text gives a formula for` `visiting classes at 2 hours` `visiting classes at 3 hours` IF
    `visiting classes at 2 hours` EQUALS 0 OR `visiting classes at 3 hours` EQUALS 0

`a mixed school has no formula` MEANS NOT `the text gives a formula for` 1 1
#ASSERT `a mixed school has no formula`

-- (5): a deputy at any level, a young-division coordinator included, who
-- served 8 consecutive years and was kept from serving by the system's
-- constraints carries the deputy's reward back into teaching, by the
-- average number of classes he managed in the last 3 years.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p15
GIVEN `consecutive years as deputy` IS A NUMBER, `kept from serving by the system's constraints` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries the deputy's reward into teaching` `consecutive years as deputy` `kept from serving by the system's constraints` IF
    `consecutive years as deputy` AT LEAST 8 AND `kept from serving by the system's constraints`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p15
GIVEN `classes in the last three years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `classes the carried reward is counted on` `classes in the last three years` IS
    IF count `classes in the last three years` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE sum `classes in the last three years` DIVIDED BY count `classes in the last three years`

-- (6): a permanent principal or deputy of a primary school whose classes
-- fell when grades 7-8 moved to the middle school keeps the reward he had.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p16
GIVEN `permanent` IS A BOOLEAN, `classes lost to the middle school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reward before` IS A NUMBER, `reward by the reduced classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the management reward after the move` `permanent` `classes lost to the middle school` `reward before` `reward by the reduced classes` IS
    IF `permanent` AND `classes lost to the middle school`
    THEN `reward before`
    ELSE `reward by the reduced classes`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p17 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p18 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p19 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p20 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p21 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.6.1.
-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p22 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p23 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p24 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_1/p25 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.6.1, continued.

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2 The heading of §7.3.6.2 (telephone reward).

-- 7.3.6.2(1): from 1.4.00 a deputy at any level receives a sum instead of
-- the 150 calls he had, pro rata to the position and the period worked, up
-- to one position; the sum is an input. (2): primary school deputies apply
-- to the Ministry's district offices, post-primary deputies to the owner.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2__para_1
GIVEN `the sum for a full position and period` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `share of the period worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the telephone sum` `the sum for a full position and period` `position fraction` `share of the period worked` IS
    `the sum for a full position and period` TIMES min `position fraction` 1 TIMES `share of the period worked`

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2__para_2
GIVEN `primary education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `7.3 party`
DECIDE `where the telephone request is made` `primary education` IS
    IF `primary education` THEN `the Ministry's district office` ELSE `the school's owner`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_2/p3 The sources (אסמכתא) of §7.3.6.2.

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3 The heading of §7.3.6.3 (travel expenses).

-- 7.3.6.3(1): from 1.9.84 a deputy, or a middle or upper division head,
-- with a car registered in his name or his wife's and a valid licence is
-- refunded as a personal car owner; (2) otherwise actual travel costs, as
-- reported; the Accountant General's rules on a personal car apply to them
-- in full. F-7.3-k: "על שמו או על שם אשתו" — a deputy whose car is
-- registered in her husband's name is not named; read as the spouse's name.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3__para_1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3__para_2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3__para_2/p2
DECLARE `car registration` IS ONE OF
    `in the deputy's own name`
    `in his wife's name`
    `in her husband's name`
    `no car`

DECLARE `travel refund` IS ONE OF
    `as a personal car owner`
    `actual travel costs, as reported`

GIVEN r IS A `car registration`, `valid driving licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `travel refund`
DECIDE `the travel refund` r `valid driving licence` IS
    IF (r EQUALS `in the deputy's own name` OR r EQUALS `in his wife's name` OR r EQUALS `in her husband's name`)
       AND `valid driving licence`
    THEN `as a personal car owner`
    ELSE `actual travel costs, as reported`

GIVETH A LIST OF `car registration`
DECIDE `the registrations 7.3.6.3 names` IS
    LIST `in the deputy's own name`, `in his wife's name`

`a car in the husband's name is not named` MEANS
    NOT (elem `in her husband's name` `the registrations 7.3.6.3 names`)
#ASSERT `a car in the husband's name is not named`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_6_3/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of §7.3.6.3.

§§ `7.3.10 ותק בניהול`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10__para_1 §7.3.10's heading and (1), a pointer to §7.6.10, encoded there.

-- (2): a deputy appointed principal carries 50% of his seniority as deputy,
-- for the seniority addition in management only; half a year rounds up to
-- a whole year; from 1.9.84, replacing every earlier arrangement. The same
-- rule as §7.6.10(7), in the same words.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10__para_2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10__para_2/p2
GIVEN `years as deputy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `management seniority carried from the deputyship` `years as deputy` IS
    `to the nearest whole` (0.5 TIMES `years as deputy`)

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_3__ssec_7_3_10/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of §7.3.10.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples (placeholder posts).
`a deputy in a primary school` MEANS
    `deputy post` WITH
        `institution`                            IS `primary school`
        `teacher's work unit in the institution` IS 30
        `teaching hours`                         IS 12
        `management hours`                       IS 18

`a manager aged 52 at the reform` MEANS
    `reform-affected manager` WITH
        `classes lost to the middle school`         IS TRUE
        `day of the reform`                         IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970
        `age on the day of the reform`              IS 52
        `management hours before`                   IS 10
        `teaching hours before`                     IS 14
        `management hours the reduced school gives` IS 6

`a manager aged 40 at the reform` MEANS
    `reform-affected manager` WITH
        `classes lost to the middle school`         IS TRUE
        `day of the reform`                         IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970
        `age on the day of the reform`              IS 40
        `management hours before`                   IS 10
        `teaching hours before`                     IS 14
        `management hours the reduced school gives` IS 6

#ASSERT `the deputy's work unit is made up as required` `a deputy in a primary school`
#ASSERT `maximum management hours` `a deputy in a primary school` EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `management hours after the reform` `a manager aged 40 at the reform` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `teaching hours after the reform` `a manager aged 40 at the reform` EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `management hours after the reform` `a manager aged 52 at the reform` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `keeps his position base in teaching and management hours as before the move` `a manager aged 52 at the reform` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 1992)
#ASSERT NOT `keeps his position base in teaching and management hours as before the move` `a manager aged 52 at the reform` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 1991)
#ASSERT `deputies the printed rows allow` `post-primary school including a middle school` 19 EQUALS 2

-- The adopted reading agrees with every printed row.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `deputies the institution may have` `primary school` n EQUALS `deputies the printed rows allow` `primary school` n)
            (range 0 38)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `deputies the institution may have` `teacher training institution` n EQUALS `deputies the printed rows allow` `teacher training institution` n)
            (range 0 27)
#ASSERT `deputies the institution may have` `primary school` 39 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `classes counted for deputies` 24 4 EQUALS 20

#TRACE `the internal committee's recommendations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the selection committee` DOES `submit recommendations to the district manager` AT 18
-- 2.2.2: the recommendations are in time on 21 March (day 20) and late on
-- 22 March.
#TRACE `the internal committee's recommendations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the selection committee` DOES `submit recommendations to the district manager` AT 20
#TRACE `the internal committee's recommendations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the selection committee` DOES `submit recommendations to the district manager` AT 21

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: every kind of
-- institution; work units of 0 to 40 hours split every way between
-- teaching and management; every reform-affected manager (classes lost or
-- not, aged 49 to 51, reformed the day before or the day of 1.9.69, 0 to 6
-- management hours before and 0 to 6 that the reduced school gives); the
-- day before and the day of 1.9.92; 0 to 60 classes with 0 to 4 of them in
-- the young division; and every March from 2020 to 2030.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`every kind of institution` MEANS LIST `primary school`, `post-primary school including a middle school`, `independent middle school`, `special education school`, `teacher training institution`

GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`, u IS A NUMBER, t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `deputy post`
DECIDE `a checked post` k u t IS
    `deputy post` WITH
        `institution`                            IS k
        `teacher's work unit in the institution` IS u
        `teaching hours`                         IS t
        `management hours`                       IS u MINUS t

GIVEN l IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE, a IS A NUMBER, mb IS A NUMBER, mr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `reform-affected manager`
DECIDE `a checked manager` l d a mb mr IS
    `reform-affected manager` WITH
        `classes lost to the middle school`         IS l
        `day of the reform`                         IS d
        `age on the day of the reform`              IS a
        `management hours before`                   IS mb
        `teaching hours before`                     IS 14
        `management hours the reduced school gives` IS mr

`every reform day checked` MEANS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1968, DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1969, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969

-- 7.3.1(1) over every kind and every split of a 0–40 hour unit: the
-- minimum is 12, 10 or 4; a post is made up as required exactly when it
-- teaches at least that minimum; and then its management hours never pass
-- the maximum of (1)'s second paragraph, which is never negative where the
-- unit holds the minimum.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                    elem (`minimum teaching hours of a deputy` k) (LIST 12, 10, 4)
                AND all (GIVEN u YIELD
                            all (GIVEN t YIELD
                                    LET d MEANS `a checked post` k u t
                                    IN      `the deputy's work unit is made up as required` d
                                            EQUALS (t AT LEAST `minimum teaching hours of a deputy` k)
                                        AND ((NOT `the deputy's work unit is made up as required` d)
                                             OR (    d's `management hours` AT MOST `maximum management hours` d
                                                 AND `maximum management hours` d AT LEAST 0)))
                                (range 0 u))
                        (range 0 40))
            `every kind of institution`

-- (2)א–ב over every manager: management hours never rise and never go
-- below zero; teaching hours never fall; what management loses teaching
-- gains, hour for hour; one whose classes were not lost, or whom (2)ב
-- protects, keeps both.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                all (GIVEN d YIELD
                        all (GIVEN a YIELD
                                all (GIVEN mb YIELD
                                        all (GIVEN mr YIELD
                                                LET m MEANS `a checked manager` l d a mb mr
                                                IN      `management hours after the reform` m AT MOST mb
                                                    AND `management hours after the reform` m AT LEAST 0
                                                    AND `teaching hours after the reform` m AT LEAST 14
                                                    AND `management hours after the reform` m PLUS `teaching hours after the reform` m
                                                        EQUALS mb PLUS 14
                                                    AND ((l AND NOT `(2)ב protects his management and teaching hours` m)
                                                         OR `management hours after the reform` m EQUALS mb))
                                            (range 0 6))
                                    (range 0 6))
                            (LIST 49, 50, 51))
                    `every reform day checked`)
            `both booleans`

-- 7.3.2(1)'s printed rows meet with no hole and no overlap: each row's
-- upper bound is one below the next row's lower bound, which is the
-- threshold the table encodes (primary 12–20, 21–29; post-primary and
-- special education 10–18, 19–27; teacher training 7–13, 14–20).
`the printed rows meet with no hole and no overlap` MEANS
        (`thresholds for` `primary school`)'s `classes for a second deputy` EQUALS 20 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `primary school`)'s `classes for a third deputy` EQUALS 29 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `post-primary school including a middle school`)'s `classes for a second deputy` EQUALS 18 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `post-primary school including a middle school`)'s `classes for a third deputy` EQUALS 27 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `special education school`)'s `classes for a second deputy` EQUALS 18 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `special education school`)'s `classes for a third deputy` EQUALS 27 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `teacher training institution`)'s `classes for a second deputy` EQUALS 13 PLUS 1
        AND (`thresholds for` `teacher training institution`)'s `classes for a third deputy` EQUALS 20 PLUS 1
#ASSERT `the printed rows meet with no hole and no overlap`

-- 7.3.2(1) over every kind and 0 to 60 classes: the printed rows give 0
-- to 3 deputies; neither they nor the adopted reading of "וכן הלאה" ever
-- give fewer deputies for more classes; the reading agrees with the rows
-- wherever they give fewer than three, and never gives fewer than they do.
-- F-7.3-a over the same space: the rows give three from the third
-- threshold on, so they leave every school past the third step without
-- an answer for a fourth deputy, in every kind of institution.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                all (GIVEN n YIELD
                            `deputies the printed rows allow` k n AT LEAST 0
                        AND `deputies the printed rows allow` k n AT MOST 3
                        AND `deputies the printed rows allow` k n AT MOST `deputies the printed rows allow` k (n PLUS 1)
                        AND `deputies the institution may have` k n AT MOST `deputies the institution may have` k (n PLUS 1)
                        AND `deputies the institution may have` k n AT LEAST `deputies the printed rows allow` k n
                        AND ((`deputies the printed rows allow` k n EQUALS 3)
                             OR `deputies the institution may have` k n EQUALS `deputies the printed rows allow` k n))
                    (range 0 60))
            `every kind of institution`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET t MEANS `thresholds for` k
                    step MEANS t's `classes for a third deputy` MINUS t's `classes for a second deputy`
                IN      `deputies the printed rows allow` k (t's `classes for a third deputy` PLUS step) EQUALS 3
                    AND `deputies the institution may have` k (t's `classes for a third deputy` PLUS step) EQUALS 4)
            `every kind of institution`

-- The note to (1)א over 0 to 60 classes with 0 to 4 in the young division:
-- the classes counted are never negative and never more than the school's;
-- a larger young division never gives the school more deputies.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN y YIELD
                            `classes counted for deputies` (n PLUS y) y EQUALS n
                        AND `classes counted for deputies` (n PLUS y) y AT MOST n PLUS y
                        AND `deputies the institution may have` `primary school` (`classes counted for deputies` (n PLUS 4) (y PLUS 1))
                            AT MOST `deputies the institution may have` `primary school` (`classes counted for deputies` (n PLUS 4) y))
                    (range 0 3))
            (range 0 60)

-- (2)ג the day before and the day of 1.9.92: the position base is kept
-- exactly from that day, for one aged 50 or more whose classes moved.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                all (GIVEN a YIELD
                            `keeps his position base in teaching and management hours as before the move` (`a checked manager` l (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970) a 10 6) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1992)
                            EQUALS (l AND a AT LEAST 50)
                        AND NOT `keeps his position base in teaching and management hours as before the move` (`a checked manager` l (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970) a 10 6) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1992))
                    (LIST 49, 50, 51))
            `both booleans`

-- F-7.3-c: 7.3.1(1) gives a figure to "grades 1–14" and another to an
-- independent middle school, whose grades (7–9) are among them. Over every
-- kind of institution, the one the two figures both reach is the
-- independent middle school, and they differ there.
GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its grades are among grades 1 to 14` k IF
    NOT (k EQUALS `teacher training institution`)

GIVEN k IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `7.3.1(1) names a figure of its own for it` k IF
    k EQUALS `independent middle school` OR k EQUALS `teacher training institution`

`the 12-hour and the 10-hour rule both reach an independent middle school` MEANS
        `its grades are among grades 1 to 14` `independent middle school`
    AND `7.3.1(1) names a figure of its own for it` `independent middle school`
    AND NOT (`minimum teaching hours of a deputy` `independent middle school` EQUALS 12)
#ASSERT `the 12-hour and the 10-hour rule both reach an independent middle school`
#ASSERT filter (GIVEN k YIELD `its grades are among grades 1 to 14` k AND `7.3.1(1) names a figure of its own for it` k) `every kind of institution` EQUALS LIST `independent middle school`

-- F-7.3-d: "the third week of March". Read as the third seven days from
-- the 1st, it ends on 21 March every year; read as the third calendar week
-- (Sunday to Saturday, the first being the week that holds 1 March), it
-- ends on the third Saturday, 21 March less the weekday of 1 March. Over
-- every March from 2020 to 2030 the two agree exactly in the years 1 March
-- is a Sunday (2020, 2026) and part in the other nine.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of March's third calendar week` y IS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 3 y) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 y) MODULO 7))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD
                    (`the last day of March's third calendar week` y EQUALS `the last day of March's third week` y)
                    EQUALS (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 y) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0)
                AND DATE_SERIAL (`the last day of March's third calendar week` y) AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 y)
                AND DATE_SERIAL (`the last day of March's third calendar week` y) AT MOST DATE_SERIAL (`the last day of March's third week` y))
            (range 2020 2030)
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN y YIELD NOT (`the last day of March's third calendar week` y EQUALS `the last day of March's third week` y)) (range 2020 2030)) EQUALS 9

`in 2025 the third calendar week of March ends on the 15th, not the 21st` MEANS
        `the last day of March's third calendar week` 2025 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025
    AND NOT (`the last day of March's third week` 2025 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025)
#ASSERT `in 2025 the third calendar week of March ends on the 15th, not the 21st`

-- F-7.3-e: "(תחולה 1.9.69)" read as the day of the reform, against read as
-- the month the hours are paid for (as (2)ג's 1.9.92 is read). Over every
-- manager and the months 31.8.69, 1.9.69 and 1.9.70, the readings part
-- exactly for one aged 50 or more whose classes were lost in a reform
-- carried out before 1.9.69, in a month from 1.9.69 on.
GIVEN m IS A `reform-affected manager`, `the month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `(2)ב protects him in the month, read as the rule's commencement` m `the month` IF
        m's `classes lost to the middle school`
    AND m's `age on the day of the reform` AT LEAST 50
    AND (`the month` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                all (GIVEN d YIELD
                        all (GIVEN a YIELD
                                all (GIVEN mo YIELD
                                        LET m MEANS `a checked manager` l d a 10 6
                                        IN  (NOT (    (`(2)ב protects his management and teaching hours` m AND (mo `is on or after` d))
                                                  EQUALS (`(2)ב protects him in the month, read as the rule's commencement` m mo AND (mo `is on or after` d))))
                                            EQUALS (    l
                                                    AND a AT LEAST 50
                                                    AND NOT (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969))
                                                    AND (mo `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969))
                                                    AND (mo `is on or after` d)))
                                    (LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1969, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1969, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970))
                            (LIST 49, 50, 51))
                    `every reform day checked`)
            `both booleans`

`a manager aged 52 reformed in 1968 is protected in 1970 on one reading only` MEANS
    LET m MEANS `a checked manager` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1968) 52 10 6
    IN      `(2)ב protects him in the month, read as the rule's commencement` m (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1970)
        AND NOT `(2)ב protects his management and teaching hours` m
#ASSERT `a manager aged 52 reformed in 1968 is protected in 1970 on one reading only`

-- §7.3.2(2) over every candidate: every pedagogical qualification, the
-- licence in hand or not, each degree flag, and 4 to 6 years of each kind
-- of teaching. A special education deputy always meets the primary
-- threshold; no threshold but the seminary's is met with under 5 years;
-- a counselling licence, or a licence not in hand, never meets (2)ב; and a
-- Pais cluster manager is held to (2)ב (finding i).
`every pedagogical qualification` MEANS
    LIST `a certified or senior certified teacher's certificate from a recognised Israeli institution`,
         `certification by supplementary examinations`,
         `a permanent teaching licence for post-primary education`,
         `a licence to practise teaching`,
         `an Israeli university teaching certificate`,
         `an educational leadership school graduate's certificate`,
         `a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary track`,
         `a licence in educational counselling`,
         `no pedagogical qualification`

GIVEN q IS A `pedagogical qualification`, li IS A BOOLEAN, dg IS A BOOLEAN, sp IS A BOOLEAN, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `deputy candidate`
DECIDE `a checked candidate` q li dg sp y IS
    `deputy candidate` WITH
        `qualification`                      IS q
        `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline` IS li
        `holds a recognised academic degree` IS dg
        `holds at least a first degree`      IS dg
        `holds at least an M.A.`             IS dg
        `years teaching in primary or post-primary grades 7-12` IS y
        `years teaching in post-primary grades 7-12 or grades 7-8 of a primary school` IS y
        `years teaching in teacher training institutions` IS y
        `certified for special education`    IS sp

GIVEN c IS A `deputy candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualification properties hold for` c IF
        ((NOT (`meets the threshold for a special education school deputy` c)) OR `meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c)
    AND ((NOT (`meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c)) OR c's `years teaching in primary or post-primary grades 7-12` AT LEAST 5)
    AND ((NOT (`meets the threshold for a middle or post-primary school deputy` c))
         OR (c's `licence in hand by the candidacy deadline` AND c's `qualification` EQUALS `a permanent licence or licence to practise on the post-primary track`))
    AND (NOT (c's `qualification` EQUALS `a licence in educational counselling` AND `meets the threshold for a primary school deputy` c))
    AND `meets the threshold for a Pais cluster manager` c EQUALS `meets the threshold qualifications` `independent middle school` c

#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                all (GIVEN li YIELD
                        all (GIVEN dg YIELD
                                all (GIVEN sp YIELD
                                        all (GIVEN y YIELD `the qualification properties hold for` (`a checked candidate` q li dg sp y))
                                            (LIST 4, 5, 6))
                                    `both booleans`)
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `every pedagogical qualification`

-- (3) 2.3.1 over every combination: an external selection is held exactly
-- when the internal one did not end in an approved candidate; 2.2.1: the
-- two-member committee recommends only when both do (finding g).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD
                all (GIVEN b YIELD
                        all (GIVEN c YIELD
                                    `an external selection is held` a b c EQUALS NOT (a AND b AND c)
                                AND `the internal committee recommends` a b EQUALS (a AND b))
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- (5) 3.4 over every split of the six voting members: the majority
-- decides, and the chair's vote only on a tie.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN ch YIELD
                        LET g MEANS 6 MINUS f
                        IN  `the Pais committee selects` f g ch
                            EQUALS (IF f EQUALS g THEN ch ELSE f GREATER THAN g))
                    `both booleans`)
            (range 0 6)

-- 7.3.4(3)-(5) over every case: the authority read is always one the text
-- gives, and the text gives two exactly within a trial year (finding j).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                all (GIVEN w YIELD
                            elem (`who may remove the deputy` t w) (`the authorities the text gives` t w)
                        AND (count (`the authorities the text gives` t w) EQUALS 2) EQUALS (t AND w))
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- 7.3.6.1(1א) over 0 to 60 standard hours and 0 to 4 visiting classes of
-- each kind: the classes never fall with more hours or classes, and are
-- the least whole number covering the hours.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                all (GIVEN v2 YIELD
                        all (GIVEN v3 YIELD
                                all (GIVEN up YIELD
                                        LET n MEANS `classes of a maritime or agricultural school` h v2 v3 up
                                            w MEANS (IF up THEN 30 ELSE 24)
                                        IN      n TIMES w AT LEAST h PLUS v2 PLUS v3 TIMES 1.5
                                            AND (n MINUS 1) TIMES w LESS THAN h PLUS v2 PLUS v3 TIMES 1.5
                                            AND n AT MOST `classes of a maritime or agricultural school` (h PLUS 1) v2 v3 up
                                            AND n AT MOST `classes of a maritime or agricultural school` h (v2 PLUS 1) v3 up
                                            AND n AT MOST `classes of a maritime or agricultural school` h v2 (v3 PLUS 1) up)
                                    `both booleans`)
                            (range 0 4))
                    (range 0 4))
            (range 0 60)

-- 7.3.6.1(1),(4) and 7.3.3(4): an uncertified deputy gets half the
-- certified one's reward; a sixth in guidance only adds. 7.3.6.2: the
-- telephone sum never passes one full position's, whatever the fraction.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET p MEANS k DIVIDED BY 20
                IN      `a deputy's management reward` 10000 p FALSE 1 TIMES 2 EQUALS `a deputy's management reward` 10000 p TRUE 1
                    AND `a deputy's rewards with guidance` 1000 600 TRUE AT LEAST `a deputy's rewards with guidance` 1000 600 FALSE
                    AND `the telephone sum` 500 (k DIVIDED BY 10) 1 AT MOST 500)
            (range 0 20)

-- 7.3.6.3 over every registration and licence: the personal-car refund
-- needs a registered car and a valid licence; the husband's name is the
-- reading adopted (finding k).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                all (GIVEN li YIELD
                        (`the travel refund` r li EQUALS `as a personal car owner`)
                        EQUALS (li AND NOT (r EQUALS `no car`)))
                    `both booleans`)
            (LIST `in the deputy's own name`, `in his wife's name`, `in her husband's name`, `no car`)

-- 7.3.10(2) over 0 to 30 years as deputy: half, a half year rounded up;
-- never more than the years served.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD
                LET c MEANS `management seniority carried from the deputyship` y
                IN      c TIMES 2 AT LEAST y
                    AND c TIMES 2 AT MOST y PLUS 1
                    AND c AT MOST y)
            (range 0 30)
